### 1.3 Grounded Citation Linker & "Cite at Cursor"

#### Purpose
Enables seamless flow from legal discovery directly into the advocate's pleading.

#### Workflow:
1. When viewing any precedent in Search Results, Similar Cases, or Verdict Anatomy, an advocate clicks **"Cite at Cursor"**.
2. If [`LegalEditor.tsx`](file:///e:/Projects/Suits/frontend/src/components/document/LegalEditor.tsx) is open, the system injects a formatted Indian court submission at the current cursor position:
   ```html
   <p style="text-indent: 40px; margin-bottom: 12px; text-align: justify;">
     That the legal proposition is firmly settled by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in 
     <b><i>State of Punjab v. Baldev Singh</i>, (1999) 6 SCC 172</b>, wherein the Constitution Bench laid down:
   </p>
   <blockquote style="margin: 12px 40px; font-style: italic; border-left: 2px solid #c5a059; padding-left: 14px;">
